XSidtool v3.0 change history.
X============================
X
Xv3.0 - patchlevel 2. 19th August 1991.
X
X  * Forgot to include Makefile.dist in shar #3 or in the MANIFEST and FILES
X    files. Tidied up the "make lint" entry in Makefile.dist.
X
X  * Added in hooks for sound.
X
X  * sidtools' canvas is no longer retained by default. Introduced a
X    "canpaint" variable which is set when it's okay to draw to the sidtool
X    canvas. Added in compression of repaint events. This now gives acceptable
X    performance under OpenWindows V2 as well as V3, although it has problems
X    still in the initial canvas redraw due to the repaint procedure being
X    called twice.
X
X  * Added in a -retained command line option, which cause sidtool to use a
X    retained canvas. This improves repainting, and is ideal for people
X    running V3, or V2 with a lot of memory. The manual pages have been
X    updated accordingly.
X
X  * Added in a -maze command line option. This allows you to specify a
X    file containing a new maze layout. Details of how to construct the maze
X    are included in the README file and the manual pages.
X
X  * Added in the new copyright messages to the sidtool source files, and
X    the online credit and help screens, after discussions with Brad Myers.
X
X  * Added in Brads' address to the README and manual pages.
X
X  * Juggled the files to fit under 60Kbytes per shar. Updated MANIFEST.
X
X  * Posted to comp.sources.games.
X
Xv3.0 - patchlevel 1. 12th August 1991.
X
X  * From Jeff Blows <jeffb@Aus.Sun.COM>
X    Warp the mouse into the maze when the user presses the "New Game" button.
X
X  * Fruit values were not being updated after clearing a screens worth of
X    dots.
X
X  * "Life" screens were not being cleared correctly in the sidtool control
X    panel when you loose a life.
X
X  * The joystick direction image (which should be near the top of the maze)
X    was not being shown.
X
X  * The scores are correctly blinked when changing players or when a player
X    looses a life.
X
X  * When a screens worth of dots was cleared, the "flashing" of the terminal
X    screen was too fast.
X
X  * The speed of the game has been tuned. Should run mostly smoothly now.
X
X  * The number of players value on the property sheet was incorrect.
X
X  * On the credits screen, the speed when moving right was incorrect.
X
X  * The "The old record" line is coming up inactive.
X
X  * The following X resources have been added:
X
X      sidtool.players:        1         # Integer: number of players.
X      sidtool.skillLevel:     5         # Integer: skill level.
X      sidtool.pauseFactor:    20000     # Integer: pause factor.
X      sidtool.slugFactor:     5         # Integer: main loop slug factor.
X
X    The manuals pages have been updated to mention these.
X
X  * The following command line options have been added:
X
X      -players players  -  number of players.
X      -skill   level    -  skill level.
X      -pause   factor   -  pause factor (in microseconds).
X      -slug    factor   -  slug factor (in milliseconds).
X
X    Changed the -s command line option to -scorefile.
X
X    The manual pages have been updated to reflect these changes.
X
X  * The users' command line options are now written out correctly after a
X    "Save WorkSpace".
X
X  * Described details of how to construct mazes in a comment above the
X    default maze in main.c
X
X  * Moved the majority of the #include file to individual source files,
X    slightly speeding up the compilation.
X
X  * Linted the code removing unwanted variables and fixing up most
X    inconsistencies.
X
Xv3.0 - patchlevel 0. 9th August 1991.
X
X  * Made available internally to Sun via anonymous ftp.
END_OF_FILE
