X.\" @(#)sidtool.man 1.4 91/08/19
X.TH SIDTOOL 6 "11 August 1991"
X.SH NAME
Xsidtool \- a Pacman like game.
X.SH SYNOPSIS
X.B "sidtool
X[
X.B \-d
X] [
X.B \-maze
X.I mazefile
X] [
X.B \-pause
X.I factor
X] [
X.B \-players
X.I players
X] [
X.B \-retained
X] [
X.B \-scorefile
X.I scorefile
X] [
X.B \-skill
X.I level
X] [
X.B \-slug
X.I factor
X] [
X.B \-v
X]
X.SH DESCRIPTION
X.I sidtool
Xis a Pacman like game. It contains a graphical interface for XView.
X.LP
X.I Sidtool
Xis played by using the keyboard or the mouse to move the image of the
Xterminal screen around the maze. Running over (eating) a small dot is worth
X10 points. Eating an "idea" spot is worth 50 points. During the game, pictures
Xof fruit will be displayed in the middle of the maze. These range in value
Xfrom 100 to 5000 points depending upon how many screens worth of dots you have
Xcleared.
X.LP
XThere are four bad guys that are trying to eat you! When you eat an "idea"
Xspot, it turns the bad guys white. You can then eat them. When they are about
Xto turn back to bad guys again, they will blink. While they are white or
Xblinking, they are worth 200, 400, 800 and 1600 points. Avoid the bad guys at
Xall costs when they are not white or blinking.
X.LP
XYou get three terminal screens per game. An extra screen is awarded at 10000
Xpoints.
X.LP
XYou can move the terminal screen around the maze using the hjkl keys (similar
Xto the vi editor), or with the mouse. To go left, hit 'h'. To go down, hit 'j'.
XTo go up, hit 'k' and to go right, hit 'l'. Alternatively, you can move the
Xmouse in the direction you want to go. Sun users will also be able to use the
Xfour arrow keys on the right function pad.
X.LP
XThere are ten skill levels. Level 1 is easy, and level 10 is hard. Level 5 is
Xthe default.
X.LP
XInitially the game is running in demonstration mode. Click SELECT on the Stop
Xbutton, to display all the other controls.
X.LP
XClick SELECT on the Help button, to get a help screen describing how to play
Xthe game.
X.LP
XClick SELECT on the Props button, to display a property window allowing you to
Xchange the skill level and the number of players. Don't forget to click SELECT
Xon the Apply button to apply you new settings.
X.LP
XClick SELECT on the Scores button, to display a window containing the current
Xhigh scores for each level.
X.LP
XClick SELECT on the Quit button to terminate the game.
X.LP
XClick SELECT on the New Game button to start a new game. Note that you need to
Xtoggle the Play type from Demo to Game if you want to play a game (as opposed
Xto running in demonstration mode).
X.LP
XClick SELECT on the Continue button to continue running. This button toggles
Xbetween Continue and Stop, and is very handy for those pesky telephone calls
Xthat always seem to interrupt the game.
X.SH OPTIONS
X.TP
X.B \-d
XRun in demonstration mode only.
X.TP
X.BI \-maze " mazefile"
XSpecify a file containing a new maze layout.
X.TP
X.BI \-pause " factor"
XThe pause factor (in microseconds) for various operations. The default is
X20000.
X.TP
X.BI \-players " players"
XThe number of players to play this game of
X.I sidtool.
XThe default is 1.
X.TP
X.B \-retained
XCause
X.I sidtool
Xto use a retained canvas for the main drawing area. This improves repaint
Xperformance.
X.TP
X.BI \-score " scorefile"
XSpecify an alternate high score file to use.
X.TP
X.BI \-skill " level"
XThe skill level for this game of
X.I sidtool.
XThe range is 1 (easy) to 10 (hard). The default is 5.
X.TP
X.BI \-slug " factor"
XThe main loop slug factor (in milliseconds). This is used to try to get a
Xrealistic speed independent of the speed of the machine that
X.I sidtool
Xis running on. The default is 5.
X.TP
X.B \-v
XPrints the version number and usage message for this release of the
X.I sidtool
Xprogram.
X.SH MAZE LAYOUT
X.I Sidtool
Xhas been designed to allow you to specify alternate mazes. The maze layout
Xshould be contained in an ASCII file, and conform to the following
Xrequirements:
X.LP 
XThe maze size is fixed at 26 by 28.
X.br
XThe maze is not allowed to have any dead ends.
X.br
XAll boxes in the maze are defined by paths.
X.br
XThe upper left corner of each box is signified by a small s.
X.br
XUse the letters r,d,l,u to signify the direction to travel around boxes.
X.br
XCorners must be signified by changing the letter.
X.br
XThe tunnel start must be signified by a capital S.
X.br
XThe exit box must have the opening at the top.
X.br
XThe ghost number 0 must be started directly above this exit.
X.br
XThe exit should be signified by capital R's.
X.br
XAll ghosts except for one must start in the box.
X.br
XThe amount of time spent in the box is specified by the number which
Xshows where the ghost goes.
X.br
XSmall dots in the maze are signified by periods '.';
X.br
XLarge dots in the maze are signified by asterisks '*';
X.br
XTunnels may be on left and right.
X.br
XAll tunnels must have exits at both sides.
X.br
XThere must be a row around the entire maze defining the border.
X.br
XAll non-tunnel parts of the border must be 'x's
X.br
XThe area in the tunnel in which the ghosts go slowly is defined as the
Xarea between the exit and the first non-space character.  Thus a '.'
Xcauses the ghosts to speed up.
X.SH RESOURCES
XOn startup,
X.I sidtool
Xwill use the following X resources. These resources can be placed in all the
Xnormal X places.
X.TP 15
X.PD 0
X.B Resource:
Xsidtool.players
X.TP
X.B Values:
XNumber of players (numeric)
X.TP
X.B Description
XThe number of players to play this game of
X.I sidtool.
XThe default is 1.
X.sp
X.TP
X.B Resource:
Xsidtool.skillLevel
X.TP
X.B Values:
XSkill level (numeric)
X.TP
X.B Description
XThe skill level for this game of
X.I sidtool.
XThe range is 1 (easy) to 10 (hard). The default is 5.
X.sp
X.TP
X.B Resource:
Xsidtool.pauseFactor
X.TP
X.B Values:
XPause factor (numeric)
X.TP
X.B Description
XThe pause factor (in microseconds) for various operations. The default is
X20000.
X.sp
X.TP
X.B Resource:
Xsidtool.slugFactor
X.TP
X.B Values:
XSlug factor (numeric)
X.TP
X.B Description
XThe main loop slug factor (in milliseconds). This is used to try to get a
Xrealistic speed independent of the speed of the machine that
X.I sidtool
Xis running on. The default is 5.
X.sp
X.SH ENVIRONMENT VARIABLES
X.TP 15
